#
# pkg-config metadata for the Yices SMT solver.
#
# Two things about this file are worth knowing before editing it.
#
# Libs.private is load-bearing, not decorative. libyices.a contains Yices
# object code only, with no third-party library code in it, and carries
# unresolved references to its configured private dependencies. A static
# consumer must supply every one of them, and the list below is where
# `pkg-config --static --libs yices` gets it from. If the list is wrong or
# incomplete, a static link fails with undefined symbols in somebody else's
# code and the cause is not obvious.
#
# Order matters. GMP must come last, because the other libraries depend on it
# and a static linker resolves left to right. The generated static link rules
# keep GMP last for this reason.
#
# Kissat and CaDiCaL: a caution for static consumers.
#
# CaDiCaL and Kissat each embed a copy of Kitten and each exports its private
# symbols. Linking stock builds of both into one program can bind one solver's
# internal calls to the other's Kitten. It is silent rather than a link error,
# which is what makes it worth a comment.
#
# This is a hazard between those two libraries. It is not created by Yices,
# and it does not affect Yices' own use of Kissat: Yices calls only the public
# kissat_* API, which the workaround below does not touch.
#
# The Yices release build avoids the collision by renaming Kissat's private
# Kitten symbols before linking. The script that does it,
# scripts/rewrite-kissat-kitten-symbols.sh, is included in the Yices source
# distribution, so it is available to you as well.
#
# Link order does not isolate two libraries' same-named private symbols. It
# only determines which definition satisfies both libraries' references, so
# a collision can occur without a link error.
#
# The libkissat_yices and libcryptominisat5 entries below refer to the
# SRI-patched forks pinned for this release at commits 7e08e870 and b8c0e44b,
# respectively. Stock upstream archives are not equivalent static link inputs.
#
# If you link statically and pull in both solvers, you have two options:
#   - apply the same renaming with that script;
#   - link only one of the two.

prefix=@prefix@
exec_prefix=@exec_prefix@
libdir=@libdir@
includedir=@includedir@

Name: Yices
Description: The Yices 2 SMT solver
URL: https://yices.csl.sri.com
Version: 2.8.0
Cflags: -I${includedir}
Libs: -L${libdir} -lyices
Libs.private: @YICES_PC_PRIVATE_LIBS@
